:- module(typecheck_getarg_declared_fallback, [c/1]).
:- use_module(library(prelude)).

% A wrong-arity constructor pattern in a head. HNF still emits a
% GuardMatch plus one GuardGetArg per position, but the match is not
% emitted (the constructor is not declared at this arity), so it
% leaves no field slots behind. The following extraction therefore
% falls back to resolving the field type from the *declaration* —
% `checkGuard`'s `Nothing` branch, `getarg_declared` in the port —
% and the constructor's declared parent type `opt(_)` contradicts the
% declared argument type `int`.
%
% `typecheck_constructor_arity_head` exercises the same wrong-arity
% pattern but declares the argument as `opt(int)`, so its fallback
% unification succeeds and reports nothing. Without this test the
% whole declaration-fallback branch can be deleted with nothing
% failing. Expect YCHR-60001 alongside the arity error.
:- chr_type opt(A) ---> none ; some(A).

:- chr_constraint c(int).
c(some(X, Y)) <=> X = Y.
